FINDINGS:
1. [MINOR] src/stdlib.rs:1367-1368 — The `BUILTIN_SIGNATURES` entry for `regex_is_match` has the wrong function name in the signature string. It reads `"regex_test(text, pattern) -> yes/no, whether the pattern matches anywhere"` but the actual function is `regex_is_match` (as registered in `BUILTIN_NAMES` at line 1181 and called via `regex.is_match`). This would cause `:sighelp regex.is_match` to display the wrong name.
2. [MAJOR] tests/regex_module_test.rs — Missing test for `regex.match` returning `nothing` when there is no match. The SPEC.md (line 1445) documents this behavior: "`regex.match` searches anywhere in the text and answers a match record, or `nothing` when there is no match." The implementation at `src/stdlib.rs:946-947` correctly returns `Value::Nothing` when `expression.captures(text)` returns `None`, but neither `regex_module_test.rs` nor `stdlib_module_docs_test.rs` has an explicit test for this branch. The existing `edge_regex_empty_pattern_matches_at_zero` tests an empty pattern which *does* match (at position zero), not a pattern that fails to match.

REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 2
